    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3445",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x) = 2\\tan x,$ which of the following shows the curve $y=f(x)?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/9cd20311c0d28bc3137e4f5163c48708e039955665721be899303265ef81cfb6.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $2.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/75c63891f497378ed8e8d9282fc764a489210c89bc09e81c6e86bdff96eeceae.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I.",
